{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>You shall not.</b> This is what I mentioned: at the beginning of the Book of the Covenant, \"You saw\" (above 20:19), He warned concerning idolatry, and at the end of the Book He warns concerning idolatry, for it ends with \"for it will be a snare to you\" (v. 33). There is only this difference: at the beginning of the Book He commanded that they not make [idols] along with HaShem, and at the end of the Book of the Covenant He commanded to eradicate the idolatry found in the land of Canaan that its inhabitants made. For one who serves idolatry is as though he transgresses all the negative commandments, and no positive commandment in this world or the world to come will benefit him."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Resolved ע\"ג as 'idolatry' and ע\"ז where it appears; both abbreviations of עבודה זרה."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:45.998198940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}